{
  "requirement": "When `habeas status` or `habeas status --all` displays a Markdown table, it MUST left-align and space-pad the Definition and Evidence columns so every row, including the header and separator row, has its `|` column delimiters in the same positions. Column widths MUST be determined by the widest displayed cell in each column.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict:** The requirement is met, and a test covers it.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `render_evidence_table` in `src/markdown.rs` (marked `{impl}` for this requirement) computes each column width as the maximum cell length. The header labels `Definition` and `Evidence` count as cells, so each width is at least the label length.\n- It then writes the header, the `---` separator and every data row with the same format string. That string is `| {x:<w$} | {y:<w$} |`, which left-aligns, space-pads and keeps the `|` delimiters at the same positions in every row.\n- `status_markdown_with_options` in `src/commands.rs` (lines 86–103) renders the table through this function, for both `status` and `status --all`. The mdBook index in `src/index.rs` uses the same function.\n- Widths use `.len()`, which counts bytes, while the format width pads by characters. The two agree here because the cells are ASCII:\n  - Definition names are limited to ASCII alphanumerics and `_`, `-` and `.` (`valid_name` in `src/lib.rs`).\n  - The noun in each definition cell is ASCII.\n  - The evidence labels (`Valid`, `Missing`, `Determination false`, `FIXME`, `Invalid`) are ASCII.\n\n**Test**\n- `status_tables_align_each_column_to_its_widest_cell` in `tests/commands.rs` carries `{test}` for this requirement.\n- It runs `habeas status` and `habeas status --all` against a fixture with definitions of varying name lengths and several evidence states.\n- For each run it checks that:\n  - the table has at least one data row beyond the header and separator;\n  - every row, including the header and separator, has `|` characters at identical byte positions;\n  - each cell has exactly one leading space and its content starts there, so it is left-aligned;\n  - each column's inner width equals the widest trimmed cell in that column;\n  - the separator row cells are `---`.\n- These checks cover the requirement's main points: both commands, header and separator rows, left-alignment and widest-cell widths.\n\n**Remaining gap:** The test does not exercise non-ASCII content. That content cannot occur given the identifier and label restrictions above, so I don't count it as a gap.",
  "inputs": [
